{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792696322,"nonce":"vHAA5sgyw5OSj6qHta4UaMy6mcM=","message":"Implemented dense inactive document caches in RayDE's DocumentState adapter. CodeDocument allocates persistent CodeLine/token arrays between transient lexical allocations. Keeping those lines in inactive tabs pins mostly-empty Immix blocks. On editor disposal, the adapter copies completed text/token/state/row/bracket caches together without re-highlighting and keeps the same CodeDocument, annotations, undo history and navigation. Each document generation is packed once; unchanged revisits reuse it.\n\nIsolated native comparison on the same 32 largest tracked Haxe files:\n- Original caches: 130.7 MiB occupied GC blocks, 153.6 MiB physical after idle.\n- Repacked: 16.9 MiB blocks, 38.8 MiB physical after idle.\n- Packed as each file completes: 17.4 MiB blocks, 38.9 MiB physical after idle.\n- Timing: 18.53 ms total for all 32 cache copies; max 5.65 ms for one file. No repeated copy on unchanged tab switches.\n- Artifacts: bin/CachePackingProbe.hx, bin/cache-packing-idle/, bin/cache-packing-timed-results/.\n\nRepeated the complete native mixed-workspace run with the same runtime, native libraries and existing Rayzor executable. All 65 tabs opened and closed in the same order; no dirty documents. Before -\u003e after physical footprint in MiB:\n- Baseline 144.3 -\u003e 153.5 (fresh-process/layout variation).\n- Haxe-focused, 48 tabs, collected: 585.6 -\u003e 506.4.\n- All 65 tabs, collected: 525.9 -\u003e 440.0.\n- Closed, server stopped, collected: 395.0 -\u003e 363.3.\n- Process peak: 703.6 -\u003e 675.1.\n\nOccupied GC blocks with all 65 tabs open: 221.6 -\u003e 127.8 MiB. Node/owner counts return to baseline, and editor, document, buffer, syntax, image and canvas maps return to zero after closure. Current build.hxml and workspace recents match their original hashes. The same LSP qualification remains: 32 callbacks, zero non-null symbol answers, files still indexing at the Haxe checkpoint. Server footprint is recorded separately.\n\nThis improves the open-tab case; it does not make every active view or transient peak stay below 500 MiB. The Haxe-focused checkpoint is still ~506 MiB, and the image atlas still retains 64 MiB. Native allocator/active-view overhead and atlas invalidation remain unresolved, so this issue stays open.\n\nValidation: SNAPSHOT_ONLY=documents passes in both themes, including cache replacement, tokens and brackets, no re-highlighting, unchanged-cache reuse, folds, selection, scroll, undo/redo and saved/unsaved close/reopen behavior. Main and probe AOT builds lower every function with zero refusals. Native Main starts/exits successfully against an isolated fixture. Installed the rebuilt executable as bin/rayde and updated/re-signed bin/RayDE.app; codesign verification passes. Previous native executable retained as bin/rayde-before-cache-packing. No sibling repository edits.\n\nFull comparison artifacts: bin/mixed-workspace-packed-results/results.json, summary.json, context.json, raw per-phase vmmap mappings and heap censuses; earlier data remains bin/mixed-workspace/.","files":null}]}